                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers. Spoiler-free Review. [/h1]\n[i]Received free copy per the Steam Curator Connect program to review[/i]\n\nThis is a very good, solid escape room experience that took me approximately 2 hours to complete, although it can be finished much sooner if you know what you're doing. Movement is by teleportation and you can turn with the joystick. You can play this game seated as long as you can pick items off the ground, although it would be easier standing.\n\nI found the puzzles to be fantastic. They were logical, common sense and made you carefully observe your surroundings for clues on how to proceed. There's even a hint button in case you get stuck. The levels are broken up into three room areas where you can continue once you have escaped that level room. \n\nThe graphics were better than the average VR escape / puzzle room. You can grab most items and some you can interact with. The animations for these interactions are well done. Unlike some escape rooms, there are no cinematic cut scenes, the only messages coveyed are via text.\n\nI had fun. With a lot of these puzzle / escape rooms I'm sometimes just happy to be done with it because they can get frustrating or tedious. This one though, just gave me the satisfaction of completing a mental challenge because of the way the puzzles were constructed. My main criticism of the game is that I think it's a little too expensive given the quality + quantity of content. At this price range for an escape room, I expect better graphics or voice acting / cinematic cut scenes OR, alternatively, more content.\n\n[b]Rate 7/10.Despite the price issue, this is a really good puzzle game and I had fun so maybe it's worth getting on sale at least. [/b]",
